  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>World Bank, Poverty and Inequality Platform, release of 22 September 2026, 2021 PPP (api.worldbank.org/pip/v1), country India, national level: survey estimates at each international line and a ladder of other lines, the lineup estimates, and the survey means table. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>. National-line and multidimensional measures from the World Development Indicators, vintage <b id="prov-wdi">–</b>.</p>
        <p>Checked by hand: PIP and the World Bank's India country profile give 5.25% below $3.00 a day for 2022-23; WDI's rounded copy gives 5.3. The gate checks PIP against WDI at every survey.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Shares are converted from fractions to per cent. Counts of poor people are computed as the share times PIP's population. Rupee values of the lines are the line times PIP's own PPP factor and CPI ratio for that survey; the gate checks that the same factors turn PIP's dollar mean into its rupee survey mean.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Six comparable spells of surveys (1977-78; 1983; 1987-88; 1993-94 to 2009-10; 2011-12; 2022-23 to 2023-24), each its own file, never joined. The lineup is kept apart from the surveys, and its nowcasts after the last survey apart again. Each PIP release can revise the past.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026 from the September 2026 PIP release. Revised with each release, twice a year.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
